+# FAA Eastern Region FOIA search and ORB custody records
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01 / PD07. A newly acquired New York TRACON memorandum records a regional response to **2004-004537-EA**. It says staff reviewed material submitted to the Commission, estimated reproduction costs and identified the **FAA Technical Center in Atlantic City** as the location where ORB disk copying would have to occur. Earlier and later custody lists give different locations for the same numbered copy. These records identify specific duplication and custody trails. The executed work and final production remain unverified. [FAA memorandum, NAID 7603366](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7603366) · [Source pins and method](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## The regional response and national file copy
+
+- **N90-162, p. 1, subject and date.** The subject gives **#2004-004537-EA, July 15, 2004**. The visible date stamp reads **JUL 26 2004**. Default extraction reads **JUL 2s m**. The earlier AWA-572 letter gives **April 8 (#2004-004537)** for the incoming request. The accession inventory identifies N90-162 as a memorandum in **agency box 15, accession 237-06-0009**. Preserve the incoming date, the regional subject reference, the stamp and the extracted text separately. [Regional memorandum](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/e-Other/5-N90-162-Memo-Nation-FOIA-Request-2004-004537-EA-dated-7-26-2004.pdf#page=1) · [Accession inventory](https://www.archives.gov/files/faa-inventory.pdf) · [AWA-572](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597140)
+- **N90-162, p. 1, lines 19–34.** The memorandum reports a completed review and estimate. It says TRACON lacked the equipment capability to make ORB copies locally and included Technical Center work in the estimate. That statement provides an office, activity and case number to trace through a work order, duplication log, transfer sheet and return record. The actual inventory reviewed by the estimate, disks copied, work performed, and shipment and receipt require separate records. [Review and copying paragraphs](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/e-Other/5-N90-162-Memo-Nation-FOIA-Request-2004-004537-EA-dated-7-26-2004.pdf#page=1)
+- **AWA-572, p. 1 concurrence panel.** The **OFFICIAL FILE COPY** contains **ARC-3**, **ATO**, **ATO-R** and **AGC-50** boxes. The visually read **ARC-3** date is **11-5-04** and the **ATO-R** date reads **11/10/04**. Default extraction for the ARC-3 date is **1/-5 -Oi**. These are concurrence-panel observations on the file copy. Seek the routing entry, approved outgoing version and receipt to determine what was sent. The initial-response paragraph addresses the separate **August** request, **2004-007463**. [File copy, p. 1](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/2-UAL-93/e-Other/2-AWA-572-Letter-FAA-Response-to-Kreindler-and-Kreindler-FOIA-Requests.pdf#page=1) · [Previous packet accounting](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a08578388e41fee10d66c4b15ecbe77d9ae83abd/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-awa572-response-packet-copies-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## The estimate has two distinct arithmetic questions
+
+The visible rows list **$2,960.00** for audio-tape reproduction, **$2,368.00** for photocopying, **$1,332.00** for ORB disk reproduction and **$980.00** for per diem. They add to **$7,640.00**. The printed total is **$7,580.00**, a difference of **$60.00**. The first check assumed that the printed total would balance. That assertion failed, and the reproducible comparison now preserves both figures. [Estimate, pp. 1–2](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/e-Other/5-N90-162-Memo-Nation-FOIA-Request-2004-004537-EA-dated-7-26-2004.pdf#page=1) · [Decimal arithmetic](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+The first two labor rows list **2 specialists**, **$37.00**, and **40** and **32** under **TOTAL HOURS**. Their printed costs match multiplication by the specialist count as well as by hours and rate. Hours times rate alone gives **$1,480.00** and **$1,184.00** for those rows. Keep the column label, row inputs and calculations together. The actual hours basis, estimating worksheet, authorization and any later charges remain open. [Estimate, pp. 1–2](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/e-Other/5-N90-162-Memo-Nation-FOIA-Request-2004-004537-EA-dated-7-26-2004.pdf#page=1)
+
